An invitation's join link carries the house's address and certificate, the
member's name and, where it has one, a claim the person chooses their password
with. Every address a screen is opened at was written to the router's log on
the phone, which is kept as a file with the app's data and travels with its
backups, and the iOS debug log is a file there too; a deep link was written to
both, and to the platform's log, whole. Each now writes an address only up to
its `?`, so nothing a link carries after it is written down anywhere.

--- a/vendor/nativephp/mobile/src/Edge/NativeRouter.php
+++ b/vendor/nativephp/mobile/src/Edge/NativeRouter.php
@@ -44 +44 @@
-        @file_put_contents($logPath, date('[H:i:s.').substr(microtime(), 2, 3).'] '.$msg."\n", FILE_APPEND);
+        @file_put_contents($logPath, date('[H:i:s.').substr(microtime(), 2, 3).'] '.preg_replace('/\?\S*/', '?', $msg)."\n", FILE_APPEND);
